{%- comment -%}
  MCP `tasks/update` (Tasks extension, "Task Update Requests"). Carries the client's
  `inputResponses` to a task in `input_required`. Approval tasks never ask the client
  for input — the decision belongs to an operator — so no response is ever outstanding
  and the server ignores them, as the extension requires, then acknowledges with an
  empty result. The request cannot change the task: an agent can never approve its
  own action. Self-scoped (tasks/find_owned).

  @param {object} params  - { taskId, inputResponses }
  @param {object} headers - context.headers (bearer identity)
  @return {object} {} | { _error:{code,message} }
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function found = 'modules/mcp/commands/tasks/find_owned', params: params, headers: headers
  unless found._error == blank
    return found
  endunless

  assign ack = {}
  return ack
%}
